IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-interpretation`
IMPORT `sfaa-div1-directors`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, Part 7 Division 1: a corporation's power to require disclosure of beneficial interest in its voting shares (section 137F)
-- and the corporation's own duty to disclose what it is told (Subdivision (3), section 137G).
-- "Corporation" is the body of section 130(2); "member" is section 130(4)'s, supplied by the caller as the answer of `s 130(4) the person is a member of the corporation`.
-- A "reasonable time" is the person's own judgment and an input. The Authority's prescriptions (content, form, manner) are not in the text and are inputs too.

§ `s 137F: power of a corporation to require disclosure of beneficial interest in its voting shares`

-- Subsection (1): a power, so a gate that fails answers NOTHING (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12). The chapeau is one function; paragraphs (a) and (b) say what the notice may ask.
-- src:28714 | 137F.—(1) Any corporation may by written notice require any
-- src:28715 | member of the corporation within such reasonable time as is specified
-- src:28716 | in the notice —
@ref s 137F(1) (src:28714-28716)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(4) answer for the person (a member of the corporation)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(1) the corporation may require the member to give the information` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` AND (`the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND `the requirement is made by written notice` AND `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any corporation may by written notice require any member of the corporation within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice"

-- src:28718 | (a) to inform it whether the member holds any voting shares in
-- src:28719 | the corporation as beneficial owner or as trustee; and
@ref s 137F(1)(a) (src:28718-28719)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(4) answer for the person (a member of the corporation)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(1)(a) the corporation may require the member to inform it whether the member holds voting shares as beneficial owner or as trustee` MEANS
    `s 137F(1) the corporation may require the member to give the information` `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- src:28724 | (b) if the member holds them as trustee, to indicate so far as the
-- src:28725 | member can the persons for whom the member holds them
-- src:28726 | (either by name or by other particulars sufficient to enable
-- src:28727 | those persons to be identified) and the nature of their
-- src:28728 | interest.
@ref s 137F(1)(b) (src:28724-28728)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(4) answer for the person (a member of the corporation)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
    `the member holds voting shares in the corporation as trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the member hold the voting shares in the corporation as trustee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(1)(b) the corporation may require the member who holds the shares as trustee to indicate the persons for whom the member holds them` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the member holds voting shares in the corporation as trustee`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the member holds them as trustee"; a function named for a power whose "if" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1)
        OTHERWISE `s 137F(1) the corporation may require the member to give the information` `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- Subsection (2): a further notice to a person the first answers name. "Where ... the corporation may": a gated power. SPLIT-SITE (ii), fork line B7:
-- the grant ruling of 2026-11-12 answers NOTHING when the gate fails; the periods ruling (b) would answer JUST FALSE.
-- src:28732 | (2) Where a corporation is informed pursuant to a notice given to
-- src:28733 | any person under subsection (1) or under this subsection that any
-- src:28734 | other person has an interest in any of the voting shares in the
-- src:28735 | corporation, the corporation may by written notice require that other
-- src:28736 | person within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice —
@ref s 137F(2) (src:28732-28736)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the corporation has been informed that the person has an interest in voting shares in the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been informed, pursuant to a notice given to any person under section 137F(1) or (2), that the person has an interest in any of the voting shares in the corporation?
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(2) the corporation may require the other person to give the information` MEANS
    IF `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` AND `the corporation has been informed that the person has an interest in voting shares in the corporation` AND `the requirement is made by written notice` AND `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): SPLIT-SITE (ii) "Where a corporation is informed pursuant to a notice given to any person under subsection (1) or under this subsection that any other person has an interest in any of the voting shares in the corporation, the corporation may by written notice require that other person"

