-- src:28755 | particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it.
@ref s 137F(3) (the particulars) (src:28749-28755)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 130(4) answer for the person (a member of the corporation)? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the requirement is made by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the requirement made by written notice?
    `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice specify a time for the answer that is reasonable?
    `the voting rights carried by voting shares held by the member are the subject of an agreement or arrangement under which another person is entitled to control the member's exercise of them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any of the voting rights carried by voting shares in the corporation held by the member the subject of an agreement or arrangement under which another person is entitled to control the member's exercise of those rights?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(3) the corporation may require the member to give particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the voting rights carried by voting shares held by the member are the subject of an agreement or arrangement under which another person is entitled to control the member's exercise of them`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "and, if so, to give particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it"; a function named for a power whose "if" gate failed (the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1)
        OTHERWISE `s 137F(3) the corporation may require the member to inform it whether the voting rights are subject to an agreement or arrangement` `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` `the person is a member of the corporation as section 130(4) reads it` `the requirement is made by written notice` `the notice specifies a reasonable time for the answer`

-- Subsection (4): the content and delivery of the notice are the Authority's to prescribe, so what they are is an input (the same pattern as section 133(3)(a)).
-- src:28759 | (4) The notice referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (3) must contain
-- src:28760 | such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the
-- src:28761 | delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the
-- src:28762 | Authority may prescribe.
@ref s 137F(4) (src:28759-28762)
GIVEN
    `the Authority has prescribed other information and requirements for the notice and its delivery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority prescribed other information that the notice must contain, and requirements for its delivery?
    `the notice contains the information the Authority prescribes and its delivery complies with the requirements the Authority prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice contain the other information the Authority prescribes, and does its delivery comply with the requirements the Authority prescribes?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(4) the notice contains the other information the Authority prescribes and is delivered as it prescribes` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Authority has prescribed other information and requirements for the notice and its delivery`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "such other information as the Authority may prescribe"
        IF `the notice contains the information the Authority prescribes and its delivery complies with the requirements the Authority prescribes`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must contain such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the Authority may prescribe"

-- Subsection (5): the duty to comply. It is class-limited ("Any person to whom a notice is issued"), so a person with no notice is outside it: NOTHING.
-- Whether a notice that fails subsection (4) still binds is a question the text does not answer (fork register B8): the duty is read as triggered by the issue of the notice.
-- src:28766 | (5) Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2)
-- src:28767 | or (3) must comply with that notice.
@ref s 137F(5) (src:28766-28767)
GIVEN
    `a notice has been issued to the person under section 137F(1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice been issued to the person under section 137F(1), (2) or (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(5) the person must comply with the notice` MEANS
    IF `a notice has been issued to the person under section 137F(1), (2) or (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2) or (3)"

DECLARE `s 137F action` IS ONE OF
    `s 137F comply with the notice`

-- "Within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice": the number of days the notice allows is an input and the rule's window.
-- src:28714 | 137F.—(1) Any corporation may by written notice require any
-- src:28715 | member of the corporation within such reasonable time as is specified
-- src:28716 | in the notice —
-- src:28718 | (a) to inform it whether the member holds any voting shares in
-- src:28719 | the corporation as beneficial owner or as trustee; and
-- src:28724 | (b) if the member holds them as trustee, to indicate so far as the
-- src:28725 | member can the persons for whom the member holds them
-- src:28726 | (either by name or by other particulars sufficient to enable
-- src:28727 | those persons to be identified) and the nature of their
-- src:28728 | interest.
-- src:28732 | (2) Where a corporation is informed pursuant to a notice given to
-- src:28733 | any person under subsection (1) or under this subsection that any
-- src:28734 | other person has an interest in any of the voting shares in the
-- src:28735 | corporation, the corporation may by written notice require that other
-- src:28736 | person within such reasonable time as is specified in the notice —
-- src:28738 | (a) to inform it whether that other person holds that interest as
-- src:28739 | beneficial owner or as trustee; and
-- src:28741 | (b) if that other person holds it as trustee, to indicate so far as
-- src:28742 | that other person can the persons for whom that other
-- src:28743 | person holds it (either by name or by other particulars
-- src:28744 | sufficient to enable them to be identified) and the nature of
-- src:28745 | their interest.
-- src:28749 | (3) Any corporation may by written notice require any member of
-- src:28750 | the corporation to inform it, within such reasonable time as is
-- src:28751 | specified in the notice, whether any of the voting rights carried by any
-- src:28752 | voting shares in the corporation held by the member are the subject of
-- src:28753 | an agreement or arrangement under which another person is entitled
-- src:28754 | to control the member’s exercise of those rights and, if so, to give
-- src:28755 | particulars of the agreement or arrangement and the parties to it.
-- src:28759 | (4) The notice referred to in subsection (1), (2) or (3) must contain
-- src:28760 | such other information as the Authority may prescribe, and the
-- src:28761 | delivery of such notice must comply with such requirements as the
-- src:28762 | Authority may prescribe.
-- src:28766 | (5) Any person to whom a notice is issued under subsection (1), (2)
-- src:28767 | or (3) must comply with that notice.
@ref s 137F(5) (the duty as a regulative rule) (src:28714-28767)
GIVEN
    `the person` IS A Party
    `the time the notice specifies, in days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after the notice is the time that the notice specifies for the answer?
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 137F action`
`s 137F(5) the person must comply with the notice within the time it specifies` MEANS
    PARTY `the person`
    MUST `s 137F comply with the notice`
    WITHIN `the time the notice specifies, in days`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "the notice was not complied with within the time it specified (section 137F(5))"

-- Subsection (6): the corporation's duty to inscribe, "Whenever" counting as "where" (the ruling of 2026-11-05, (c)): a failed gate answers JUST FALSE.
-- src:28771 | (6) Whenever a corporation receives information from a person
-- src:28772 | pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under this section
-- src:28777 | with respect to shares held by a member of the corporation, it is under
-- src:28778 | an obligation to inscribe against the name of that member in a
-- src:28779 | separate part of the register kept by it under section 137C —
-- src:28781 | (a) the fact that the requirement was imposed and the date on
-- src:28782 | which it was imposed; and
-- src:28784 | (b) the information received pursuant to the requirement.
@ref s 137F(6) (src:28771-28784)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the corporation has received information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 137F with respect to shares held by a member` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation received information from a person, pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under section 137F, with respect to shares held by a member of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(6) the corporation must inscribe the fact of the requirement, its date and the information in a separate part of the register` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a corporation"; the body is not a corporation as section 130(2) reads the word for Division 1
        IF `the corporation has received information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 137F with respect to shares held by a member`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Whenever a corporation receives information from a person pursuant to a requirement imposed on the person under this section with respect to shares held by a member of the corporation"

