GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(7) section 137C applies to the separate part of the register` MEANS
    IF `the part of the register is the separate part referred to in section 137F(6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the part of the register referred to in subsection (6)"

-- src:28795 | (8) Any person who —
-- src:28797 | (a) intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (5); or
-- src:28799 | (b) in purported compliance with subsection (5), provides any
-- src:28800 | information which the person knows is false or misleading
-- src:28801 | in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is,
-- src:28803 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall —
-- src:28805 | (c) in the case of an individual, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28806 | not exceeding $250,000 or to imprisonment for a term not
-- src:28807 | exceeding 2 years or to both and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:28808 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:28809 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:28810 | after conviction; or
-- src:28812 | (d) in the case of a corporation, be liable on conviction to a fine
-- src:28813 | not exceeding $250,000 and, in the case of a continuing
-- src:28814 | offence, to a further fine not exceeding $25,000 for every
-- src:28815 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues
-- src:28816 | after conviction.
@ref s 137F(8) (src:28795-28816)
GIVEN
    `the person contravened section 137F(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person contravene section 137F(5)?
    `the contravention was intentional or reckless` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention intentional or reckless?
    `the person in purported compliance with section 137F(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In purported compliance with section 137F(5), did the person provide information that is false or misleading in a material particular?
    `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the person know that the information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was the person reckless as to whether it was?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137F(8) the person is guilty of an offence under subsection (8)` MEANS
    IF ((`the person contravened section 137F(5)` AND `the contravention was intentional or reckless`) OR (`the person in purported compliance with section 137F(5) provided information that is false or misleading in a material particular` AND `the person knew that information was false or misleading in a material particular, or was reckless as to whether it was`))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): SPLIT-SITE (i) the text says who is guilty ("intentionally or recklessly contravenes subsection (5)" or "provides any information which the person knows is false or misleading in a material particular or is reckless as to whether it is"), not that anyone else is innocent

@ref s 137F(8) (the penalty) (src:28795-28816)
GIVEN
    `the person is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person an individual (a natural person)?
    `the person is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a corporation (as section 2(1) defines "corporation")?
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 137F(8) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is an individual`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 24, TRUE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years (24 months) or both; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        IF `the person is a corporation`
        THEN JUST (Penalty OF 250000, 0, FALSE, 25000)  -- a fine not exceeding $250,000, no imprisonment is stated, so 0; a further fine not exceeding $25,000 a day after conviction
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the case of an individual" and "in the case of a corporation" are the only cases the paragraphs name

-- src:28820 | (9) Any person who —
-- src:28822 | (a) contravenes subsection (5); or
-- src:28827 | (b) in purported compliance with subsection (5), provides any
-- src:28828 | information which is false or misleading in a material
-- src:28829 | particular,
-- src:28831 | in circumstances other than as set out in subsection (8) shall be guilty
-- src:28832 | of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:28833 | $25,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- src:28834 | exceeding $2,500 for every day or part of a day during which the
