        IF `the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the corporation` OR `the person proves that the requirement to give the information was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the person proves that the information in question was already in the possession of the corporation or that the requirement to give it was for any other reason frivolous or vexatious"; this section gives no defence on these facts

§ `s 137G: duty of a corporation to make disclosure`

-- Paragraph (a): the notices of a director or chief executive officer that start the duty. Section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f) are named, with (g) in respect
-- of a change in the same; a matter outside the list (paragraph (e), or a related corporation's) is not named, so the answer is NOTHING.
-- Whether the notice is of the matter or of a change in it makes no difference to the list, so the change flag is not asked.
-- src:28866 | (a) a director or chief executive officer of the corporation
-- src:28867 | pursuant to a requirement imposed on him or her under
-- src:28868 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or under
-- src:28869 | section 133(1)(g) in respect of a change in the particulars
-- src:28870 | of any matter referred to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28871 | (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f); or
@ref s 137G(1)(a) (src:28866-28871)
GIVEN
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137G(1)(a) the matter is one the paragraph names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `s 133(1)(a)(i) shares in the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(b)(i) debentures of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(c)(i) rights or options in respect of the acquisition or disposal of shares in or debentures of the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(d)(i) contracts under which a person has a right to call for or make delivery of shares in the corporation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 133(1)(f) other securities or securities-based derivatives contracts the Authority prescribes` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the paragraph names section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f), and (g) in respect of a change in the same; it is silent on any other matter

-- src:28864 | 137G.—(1) Where a corporation has been notified in writing by —
-- src:28866 | (a) a director or chief executive officer of the corporation
-- src:28867 | pursuant to a requirement imposed on him or her under
-- src:28868 | section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i), (c)(i), (d)(i) or (f), or under
-- src:28869 | section 133(1)(g) in respect of a change in the particulars
-- src:28870 | of any matter referred to in section 133(1)(a)(i), (b)(i),
-- src:28871 | (c)(i), (d)(i) and (f); or
-- src:28876 | (b) a substantial shareholder in the corporation pursuant to a
-- src:28877 | requirement imposed on the substantial shareholder under
-- src:28878 | section 135, 136 or 137,
@ref s 137G(1) (the notice) (src:28864-28878)
GIVEN
    `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body a corporation to which Division 1 of Part 7 applies (the answer to the question under section 130(2): a listed company, or a corporation with a primary listing)?
    `the shares of the corporation are listed on the official list of an approved exchange` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are any or all of the shares of the corporation listed on the official list of an approved exchange?
    `the corporation has been notified in writing by a director or chief executive officer of the corporation under section 133(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been notified in writing by a director or chief executive officer of the corporation, pursuant to a requirement imposed on the director or officer under section 133(1)?
    `the matter` IS A `s 133(1) matter` @desc Which kind of matter is it: shares, debentures, rights or options, contracts, participatory interests, or other securities that the Authority prescribes, of the corporation or of a related corporation?
    `the corporation has been notified in writing by a substantial shareholder in the corporation under section 135, 136 or 137` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the corporation been notified in writing by a substantial shareholder in the corporation, pursuant to a requirement imposed under section 135, 136 or 137?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137G(1) the corporation must announce or disseminate the information stated in the notice` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the body is a corporation within section 130(2)`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a corporation"; the body is not a corporation as section 130(2) reads the word for Division 1
        IF NOT `the shares of the corporation are listed on the official list of an approved exchange`
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the approved exchange on whose official list any or all of the shares of the corporation are listed"
        IF `the corporation has been notified in writing by a substantial shareholder in the corporation under section 135, 136 or 137`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the corporation has been notified in writing by a director or chief executive officer of the corporation under section 133(1)`
        THEN `s 137G(1)(a) the matter is one the paragraph names` `the matter`
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a corporation has been notified in writing by"

-- The time: "as soon as practicable and in any case, no later than the end of the business day following the day on which the corporation received the notice".
-- "As soon as practicable" is a judgment the text does not measure, so the functions answer on the hard limit only (fork register B9).
